Origin:
Keep the microSD slot powered from the start, as before eotics
1784c8fc1d: with the rail off UEFI cannot read the card it boots from,
and the release hangs before the boot loader. The DSDT's power resource
stays and finds the rail on. farjanatech/rpi5-uefi made the same change
independently (temporary-patches/0002, a62ee0bd37).

diff --git a/Platform/RaspberryPi/RPi5/Drivers/RpiPlatformDxe/Peripherals.c b/Platform/RaspberryPi/RPi5/Drivers/RpiPlatformDxe/Peripherals.c
index 21ed8b9..e3cf8f2 100644
--- a/Platform/RaspberryPi/RPi5/Drivers/RpiPlatformDxe/Peripherals.c
+++ b/Platform/RaspberryPi/RPi5/Drivers/RpiPlatformDxe/Peripherals.c
@@ -73,8 +73,9 @@ InitGpioPinctrls (
   GpioSetFunction (BCM2712_GIO_AON, 5, GIO_AON_PIN5_ALT_SD_CARD_G);
   GpioSetPull (BCM2712_GIO_AON, 5, BCM2712_GPIO_PIN_PULL_UP);
 
-  // ACPI owns the microSD power rail and starts with it off.
-  GpioWrite (BCM2712_GIO_AON, 4, FALSE);
+  // The slot stays powered: UEFI boots from the card. ACPI's power
+  // resource takes the rail over from here and finds it on.
+  GpioWrite (BCM2712_GIO_AON, 4, TRUE);
   GpioSetDirection (BCM2712_GIO_AON, 4, BCM2712_GPIO_PIN_OUTPUT);
 
   // Default the microSD signaling voltage to 3.3 V.
